      "front": "Why does $\\text{arsinh}\\,x$ exist for every real $x$ while $\\text{arcosh}\\,x$ needs $x \\ge 1$?",
      "back": "sinh is one-to-one on the whole real line, so its inverse has no restriction. cosh is not one-to-one unless its domain is restricted to $x \\ge 0$, and that restricted branch has range $y \\ge 1$.",
